So, $A_{min}$ is a very good candidate for the top of a pair.
If we use $A_{min}$ as a top, we need to find a bottom $B$ such that $A_{min} \le B/2$. To save larger mochi for other potential top mochi (which might be larger than $A_{min}$), we should pick the smallest possible $B$ that satisfies the condition.
Why? Suppose we have a valid pairing where $A_{min}$ is not used as a top. Then $A_{min}$ is either unused or used as a bottom.
Case 1: $A_{min}$ is unused. We can potentially add a pair using $A_{min}$ as top if there is an available $B$ such that $A_{min} \le B/2$. If there is such a $B$, we should use it.
